  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot arccot(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot arccot(\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot arccot(\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{1+{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot(\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{1+x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot(\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
